From: Kryxzort <101042137+Kryxzort@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 08:49:53 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 53/97] render: particle control points take their overrides,
 scene space and the system's transform
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Decoded from wallpaper64.exe 2.8.485 (GH 0x140251f70 → 0x1402504f0, the instance table GH
0x140273180):

- instanceoverride controlpoint0..7 replace the control points' offsets unless the point follows
  the pointer or has flags 0x10004 (mask 0x10005). They are read every step, so a user property
  or a script moves the point. They weren't parsed (P10).
- Flags bit 1: the offset is in the scene's space (WE's world: y up from the bottom-left); the
  system turns it into its own space by the inverse of its whole transform. Control point 0
  ignores the bit. LWE read the offset as already centred, subtracted only the origin and applied
  the bit to point 0 too (P34).
- A pointer control point is unscaled and unrotated the same way: the cursor followers of a
  scaled or turned system sat off the cursor (P35).
- A local offset is WE's y-up particle space, mirrored like an emitter's origin; it was taken
  as is, so a point "0 8 0" went the other way from an emitter at "0 8 0" (8 library scenes have
  a control point offset with y).

Not ported: controlpointangle0..7 (the control points' rotation, which turns operator offsets
relative to them).

Origin: ours
Why: docs/player/spikes/we-lwe-gap-audit.md B11 (P10, P34, P35)
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01288H8XbjUdhpEVfhFbe7bj
